course: dictionary
lesson: 12829
title: Empowered: strong, and in charge
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Empowered means feeling strong, confident and in control of your own life. It can also mean having been given the power, right or permission to do something. Look at the clues around the word. «The school council gave us a vote, so we felt empowered.» A vote gives you a say, so empowered must mean you feel strong and in charge.
explain: The second meaning is about official power. «The police are empowered to arrest people who break the law.» Here empowered means the law gives the police the right to do it. Ask yourself: who is allowed to do what? If the sentence is about rights or permission, empowered probably means given the power to act.
explain: Notice the word inside it: power. To empower someone is to give them power. If a sentence says someone was empowered by something, look for what gave them strength, such as «Ella felt empowered by her team.» Swap in "strong and in charge" and check it still makes sense.
fact: Empowered is the past form of the verb empower, so it can describe someone who has been given power.
fact: «Empowered» means feeling strong, confident and in control of your own life.
fact: «Empowered» can also mean given the power, right or permission to do something, especially officially.
fact: «Empowered to do» means allowed to do it; «empowered by» tells you what gave you strength.
exercise: «After the school council vote, the pupils felt empowered.» What does empowered mean here? | Very cold | *Feeling strong and in control | Lost and confused | Feeling sleepy after lunch
exercise: «The park ranger is empowered to fine people who drop litter.» What does empowered mean here? | Afraid of the dark | Feeling very sad | *Given the official power or permission to do it | Tired from a long walk
exercise: Find the verb that the word empowered comes from. | emerge | tower | *empower | empty
test: «Her club leader gave her a chance to lead the project, and she felt empowered.» What does empowered most likely mean? | Lost in a crowd | Bored and unhappy | *Strong, confident and in charge | Cold and wet
test: «The judge is empowered to make the final decision.» What does this tell you? | The judge has lost the case | The judge is a child | The judge is very tired | *The judge has the official power to decide
exam: Ella says empowered means "very angry". Why is she wrong? | *Empowered means feeling strong and confident, or having the power to act | Empowered means very small | Empowered means very angry, as Ella says | Empowered means very quiet
